# PowOS's desktop packages on Android: every package the desktop image installs (dnf in
# containers/Containerfile.base-common + Containerfile), mapped to Arch Linux ARM or left out on purpose.
# check-layer-drift.sh fails when the Containerfiles install a package this file doesn't account for.
#
# Format:  + <fedora-name> <arch-package...>   installed in the phone rootfs
#          - <fedora-name> <reason>             not on Android, on purpose
#          ~ <fedora-name> <how>                provided another way (see install-powos-android.sh)

# Gaming
~ steam                        Valve's ARM64 client (steam_client_linuxarm64), Proton ARM64 + FEX via Steam
+ lutris                       lutris
- umu-launcher                 not in Arch Linux ARM (AUR); Steam runs Proton itself
- mangohud.x86_64              not in Arch Linux ARM for aarch64 (AUR only)
- mangohud.i686                32-bit x86: games' own bits come through FEX/Proton
- vkBasalt.x86_64              post-processing layer for x86 games; not packaged for aarch64
- vkBasalt.i686                same
- gamescope.x86_64             KWin is the compositor; gamescope needs DRM/KMS, which apps don't get
- gamescope-libs.x86_64        same
- gamescope-libs.i686          same
- gamescope-shaders            same
- libFAudio.x86_64             x86 game runtime: comes with Proton/FEX
- libFAudio.i686               same
- libobs_vkcapture.x86_64      OBS game capture (x86)
- libobs_vkcapture.i686        same
- libobs_glcapture.x86_64      same
- libobs_glcapture.i686        same
- VK_hdr_layer                 HDR output needs DRM/KMS
- cage                         kiosk compositor for gamescope sessions
- ds-inhibit                   Steam Deck controller inhibit
- jupiter-sd-mounting-btrfs    Steam Deck SD-card mounting
- steamdeck-kde-presets-desktop Steam Deck desktop presets
- scx-scheds                   sched_ext needs our own kernel
- scx-tools                    same

